     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\">Does this do what you want? </div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\">plot + scale_y_reverse(breaks = c(seq(1:30)))</div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Mar 25, 2015 at 11:17 AM, Paul <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">pault...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">breaks </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> c</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">seq</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">30</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span></blockquote></div><br><br></div></div>\r\n"
